commit 2fc3148f65e026d84491482d37e68594924ab2db
Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 27 18:16:50 2026 +1100

    ovn: Keep server-only imports out of the OVN agent
    
    The OVN agent imports neutron.common.ovn.utils, which imports pecan and
    the port model and object, and ovsdb_monitor, which imports the hash
    ring and router object; only the server uses them. Import them where
    used, and test the OVN agent's imports as the previous change does.
    
    With neutron-lib's "Load the DB API only for DB users" and "db: Import
    the DB API inside the functions using it", the probe shows the OVN agent
    without the DB API or pecan, down from 119 to 109MB; without the
    neutron-lib change, 4MB. The DHCP agent also needs "agent: Import the
    resource cache only for L2 agents".
    
    Prompt: Mikal asked for the neutron changes that keep the DB API out of
    the neutron agents, as three patches grouped by the agents they free.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (high effort)
    
    Change-Id: I86aad1f1e363ef11f8efd3a14282d768047b59e3
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

